# UI alignment and order

Fix alignment as part of the change. Do not wait to be asked, and do not mention alignment as a task.

- One control for one job. Do not put a button that repeats a table, sort, or list below it.
- Prices with any listed discount come first. Card offers on this search come next. Travel cards a person could apply for come last.
- Map and mood photo sit at the very end of the results, after the decisions.
- Rows share one grid: name left, amount right, meta on the line below. Same padding, same baseline.
- Name the site that honours an offer (Goibibo, MakeMyTrip, Cleartrip). Fares come from Booking.com; card codes do not apply there.
- Every card and offer row has a check/terms link.
- A primary action is enabled as soon as the values the destination site can accept are present. Do not gate Booking.com on names it cannot receive.
- Before calling a dialog or form done, type, clear, and change a number input and confirm the button state follows the values on screen.
